American crows, Corvus brachyrhynchos, cache food using spatial memory so precise they can recall thousands of hiding spots months later. You’d do well to cache your data at thirty Hertz and let them handle the rest."

Rashmi tapped her pen like a tiny baton. "Cache is fine, but I need the bandwidth. Thirty will alias my bridge vibration."

